  variables:
    # Backend required for Gitlab state
    BACKEND_TF: |
      terraform {
        backend "http" {
        }
      }
  before_script:
  - echo "$BACKEND_TF" > backend.tf

it may also interest this audience that due to gitlab's in-container shell detection scheme, often a better entrypoint override is     entrypoint: ["/usr/bin/env"]    (assuming such a thing exists, of course)

Use variables in lifecycle attributes such as prevent_destroy or ignore_changes

### OpenTofu Version

```shell
1.6.2
```


### Use Cases

The main use case is for module providers to be able to parameterize lifecycle arguements. For example preventing the destruction of a specific resource or changes to the 'ignore_changes' lifecycle argument. Dynamic lifecycle blocks would also work See below:

variable "prevent_destroy" {
  default = true
}

variable "ignore_x_change" {
  default = true
}

resource "any_resource" "main" {
  x = "aabbcc"
  lifecycle {
    prevent_destroy = "${var.prevent_destroy}"
    ignore_changes = var.ignore_x_change == true ? ["x"] : []
  }
}

### Attempted Solutions

I don't see any workarounds for this currently.

